From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: repatches <repatches@kimono.invalid>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:15:02 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] mobile: Give the app Kimono Photos' identity

The app installs as its own app, beside the official Immich app if someone
has both, and every name a person sees says Kimono Photos.

Must survive upstream changes:
- Android applicationId app.kimono.photos (the Kotlin namespace stays
  app.alextran.immich so upstream's classes don't move); launcher label and
  share/view intent labels say "Kimono Photos".
- iOS bundle ids and App Group come from ios/Signing.xcconfig:
  app.kimono.photos / app.kimono.photos.dev / group.app.kimono.photos, team
  left empty (CI passes DEVELOPMENT_TEAM). Display name "Kimono Photos".
- Link scheme kimono-photos:// replaces immich:// everywhere it is declared
  or built (manifest, Info.plist, router, home-screen widgets).
- OAuth callback scheme app.kimono.photos:///oauth-callback replaces
  app.immich:///oauth-callback; Kimono registers it as a redirect URI.
- Immich's my.immich.app universal links are removed (domain we don't own).

